From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: grow the BO when a tiled image converts to linear

A 2D image overwritten whole a few times is switched from tiled to linear
in panfrost_ptr_unmap, into the BO it already had, on the assumption that
the linear layout is never bigger. Linear rows are padded to 64 bytes and
tiled images to 16 pixels, so a narrow 8-bit image can need more: a 400x300
R8 texture goes from 121,600 to 134,400 bytes. The copy then runs past the
BO (the assert is compiled out), and the next upload faults at the end of
the mapping. SDL's IYUV streaming textures (three 8-bit planes updated every
frame) hit this on a Mali-G31.

Allocate a BO of the linear size when the old one is too small, as the
shadow path of panfrost_ptr_map does; if that fails, keep the image tiled.

Signed-off-by: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -2366,17 +2366,43 @@
                panfrost_resource_setup(screen, prsrc, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
                                        prsrc->image.props.format, 0);
 
-               /* converting the resource from tiled to linear and back
-                * shouldn't increase memory usage...
-                */
-               assert(prsrc->plane.layout.data_size_B <= panfrost_bo_size(bo));
+               /* Linear rows are padded to 64 bytes and tiled images to 16
+                * pixels: a narrow 8-bit image can outgrow its BO */
+               bool fits =
+                  prsrc->plane.layout.data_size_B <= panfrost_bo_size(bo);
 
-               util_copy_rect(
-                  bo->ptr.cpu + prsrc->plane.layout.slices[0].offset_B,
-                  prsrc->base.format,
-                  prsrc->plane.layout.slices[0].tiled_or_linear.row_stride_B, 0,
-                  0, transfer->box.width, transfer->box.height, trans->map,
-                  transfer->stride, 0, 0);
+               if (!fits) {
+                  struct panfrost_bo *newbo = panfrost_bo_create(
+                     dev, prsrc->plane.layout.data_size_B,
+                     bo->flags & ~PAN_BO_DELAY_MMAP, bo->label);
+
+                  if (newbo && !panfrost_bo_mmap(newbo)) {
+                     panfrost_dirty_state_all(ctx);
+                     panfrost_bo_unreference(prsrc->bo);
+                     prsrc->bo = bo = newbo;
+                     prsrc->plane.base = newbo->ptr.gpu;
+                     fits = true;
+                  } else {
+                     if (newbo)
+                        panfrost_bo_unreference(newbo);
+                     panfrost_resource_setup(
+                        screen, prsrc,
+                        DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ARM_16X16_BLOCK_U_INTERLEAVED,
+                        prsrc->image.props.format, 0);
+                     prsrc->modifier_constant = true;
+                  }
+               }
+
+               if (fits) {
+                  util_copy_rect(
+                     bo->ptr.cpu + prsrc->plane.layout.slices[0].offset_B,
+                     prsrc->base.format,
+                     prsrc->plane.layout.slices[0].tiled_or_linear.row_stride_B,
+                     0, 0, transfer->box.width, transfer->box.height,
+                     trans->map, transfer->stride, 0, 0);
+               } else {
+                  panfrost_store_tiled_images(trans, prsrc);
+               }
             } else {
                panfrost_store_tiled_images(trans, prsrc);
             }
